    "title": "Bible Louis Segond avec audio",
    "description": "Free Louis Segond Bible with audio.\r\n\r\nWe created this audio version application to help you read or listen to the Free Louis Segond Bible with audio.\r\n\r\nInstall now the best Bible application to have the Holy Word on your Android smartphone or tablet.\r\n\r\nAccess your free Louis Segond Bible (LSG) wherever you are. It is an offline application, to be used even without an internet connection.\r\n\r\nThis app is yours to read and study the Bible. Take advantage of its new features:\r\n\r\nTHE FREE OFFLINE BIBLE\r\n\r\n- Louis Segond version of the Bible\r\n- It contains 66 books\r\n- Free\r\n- Friendly user interface\r\n- High quality audio: listen to the Bible with your headphones, verse by verse or the whole chapter. Adjust tone and volume\r\n\r\nUNIQUE FEATURES\r\n\r\n- Highlight verses with colors and create your own favorites list\r\n- Add notes to verses\r\n- Search by keywords\r\n- Open your phone and you will get the verse of the day\r\n- Turn verses into photos. Once your photo is created, you can share them on social networks, Facebook and Twitter.\r\n- Adjust text size\r\n- Set night mode to protect your eyes when reading at night\r\n- Easily copy and paste verses to Facebook, Twitter or Instagram\r\n- The application remembers the last paragraph read\r\n\r\nWHAT ARE THE BOOKS OF THE BIBLE Louis Segond (KJV) audio?\r\n\r\nThe Free Christian Bible is made up of two parts: the Old Testament and the New Testament.\r\n\r\nThe Old Testament is made up of 39 books: Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers, Deuteronomy, Joshua, Judges, Ruth, 1 Samuel, 2 Samuel, 1 Kings, 2 Kings, 1 Chronicles, 2 Chronicles, Ezra, Nehemiah, Esther, Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, Song of Solomon, Isaiah, Jeremiah, Lamentations, Ezekiel, Daniel, Hosea, Joel, Amos, Obadiah, Jonah, Micah, Nahum, Habakkuk, Zephaniah, Haggai, Zechariah, Malachi.\r\nThe New Testament contains texts relating to the life of Jesus. These are the Gospels (Matthew, Mark, Luke and John), the Acts of the Apostles, the Epistles and the Apocalypse.",
    "descriptionHTML": "Free Louis Segond Bible with audio.<br><br>We created this audio version application to help you read or listen to the Free Louis Segond Bible with audio.<br><br>Install now the best Bible application to have the Holy Word on your Android smartphone or tablet.<br><br>Access your free Louis Segond Bible (LSG) wherever you are. It is an offline application, to be used even without an internet connection.<br><br>This app is yours to read and study the Bible. Take advantage of its new features:<br><br>THE FREE OFFLINE BIBLE<br><br>- Louis Segond version of the Bible<br>- It contains 66 books<br>- Free<br>- Friendly user interface<br>- High quality audio: listen to the Bible with your headphones, verse by verse or the whole chapter. Adjust tone and volume<br><br>UNIQUE FEATURES<br><br>- Highlight verses with colors and create your own favorites list<br>- Add notes to verses<br>- Search by keywords<br>- Open your phone and you will get the verse of the day<br>- Turn verses into photos. Once your photo is created, you can share them on social networks, Facebook and Twitter.<br>- Adjust text size<br>- Set night mode to protect your eyes when reading at night<br>- Easily copy and paste verses to Facebook, Twitter or Instagram<br>- The application remembers the last paragraph read<br><br>WHAT ARE THE BOOKS OF THE BIBLE Louis Segond (KJV) audio?<br><br>The Free Christian Bible is made up of two parts: the Old Testament and the New Testament.<br><br>The Old Testament is made up of 39 books: Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers, Deuteronomy, Joshua, Judges, Ruth, 1 Samuel, 2 Samuel, 1 Kings, 2 Kings, 1 Chronicles, 2 Chronicles, Ezra, Nehemiah, Esther, Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, Song of Solomon, Isaiah, Jeremiah, Lamentations, Ezekiel, Daniel, Hosea, Joel, Amos, Obadiah, Jonah, Micah, Nahum, Habakkuk, Zephaniah, Haggai, Zechariah, Malachi.<br>The New Testament contains texts relating to the life of Jesus. These are the Gospels (Matthew, Mark, Luke and John), the Acts of the Apostles, the Epistles and the Apocalypse.",
